:10Z","performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/issues/comments/2679382376","html_url":"https://github.com/ericniebler/range-v3/issues/1848#issuecomment-2679382376","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/issues/1848","id":2679382376,"node_id":"IC_kwDOANpJv86ftCFo","user":{"login":"brevzin","id":13238276,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMjM4Mjc2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13238276?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brevzin","html_url":"https://github.com/brevzin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brevzin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brevzin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brevzin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brevzin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brevzin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brevzin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brevzin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brevzin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brevzin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-24T18:57:11Z","updated_at":"2025-02-24T18:57:47Z","body":"I'm not familiar with how to actually implement `stable_sort`, but it looks like the logic ends up doing something like this:\n```cpp\n    std::vector<std::string> stuff = {\"a\", \"b\", \"c\"};\n    auto cpy = stuff; // this is our temporary buffer\n\n    auto first = stuff.begin();\n    auto middle = stuff.begin() + 1;\n    auto last = stuff.end();\n\n    ranges::merge(\n        ranges::make_move_iterator(cpy.begin()),\n        ranges::make_move_iterator(cpy.begin() + 1),\n        ranges::make_move_iterator(middle),\n        ranges::make_move_iterator(last),\n        first,\n        ranges::less(),\n        ranges::identity(),\n        ranges::identity());\n\n\n    fmt::print(\"{}\\n\", stuff); // [\"a\", \"\", \"\"]\n```\n\nWhich in this specific case is basically self-move-assigning all the elements after the first. Which is why those get wiped. \n\nI wonder if the issue is `merge_adaptive` calling `merge` on overlapping ranges. ","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/issues/comments/2679382376/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"brevzin","id":13238276,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMjM4Mjc2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13238276?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brevzin","html_url":"https://github.com/brevzin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brevzin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brevzin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brevzin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brevzin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brevzin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brevzin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brevzin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brevzin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brevzin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":16436338371,"node_id":"LE_lADOANpJv86rZ0JczwAAAAPTrp7D","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/issues/events/16436338371","actor":{"login":"brevzin","id":13238276,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMjM4Mjc2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13238276?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brevzin","html_url":"https://github.com/brevzin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brevzin/followers"