blic","site_admin":false},"html_url":"https://github.com/ericniebler/range-v3","description":"Range library for C++14/17/20, basis for C++20's std::ranges","fork":false,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3","forks_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/forks","keys_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/keys{/key_id}","collaborators_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/collaborators{/collaborator}","teams_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/teams","hooks_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/hooks","issue_events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/issues/events{/number}","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/events","assignees_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/assignees{/user}","branches_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/branches{/branch}","tags_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/tags","blobs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/git/blobs{/sha}","git_tags_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/git/tags{/sha}","git_refs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/git/refs{/sha}","trees_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/git/trees{/sha}","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/statuses/{sha}","languages_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/languages","stargazers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/stargazers","contributors_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/contributors","subscribers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/subscribers","subscription_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/subscription","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/commits{/sha}","git_commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/git/commits{/sha}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/comments{/number}","issue_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/issues/comments{/number}","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/contents/{+path}","compare_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/compare/{base}...{head}","merges_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/merges","archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/{archive_format}{/ref}","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/downloads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/deployments","created_at":"2013-11-11T16:05:48Z","updated_at":"2026-09-12T13:47:48Z","pushed_at":"2026-04-12T21:47:31Z","git_url":"git://github.com/ericniebler/range-v3.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:ericniebler/range-v3.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/ericniebler/range-v3.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/ericniebler/range-v3","homepage":"","size":34288,"stargazers_count":4373,"watchers_count":4373,"language":"C++","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":false,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":true,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":466,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":286,"license":{"key":"other","name":"Other","spdx_id":"NOASSERTION","url":null,"node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTA="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":["c-plus-plus","iterator","proposal","range","range-library"],"visibility":"public","forks":466,"open_issues":286,"watchers":4373,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/pulls/1865","html_url":"https://github.com/ericniebler/range-v3/pull/1865","diff_url":"https://github.com/ericniebler/range-v3/pull/1865.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/ericniebler/range-v3/pull/1865.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Fixes #1848.\n\n## Root cause\n\nFor lengths > 256, `ranges::stable_sort` takes the buffered \"adaptive\" path (`stable_sort_adaptive` -> `merge_adaptive`). `merge_adaptive_fn::impl` moves the smaller of the two runs into a temporary buffer and merges it back with the larger, unbuffered run, writing the result starting at the beginning of the unbuffered run's original storage — i.e. the *output* range aliases one of the *input* ranges (this is the standard in-place-merge-with-buffer trick).\n\n`impl` delegated this merge to the generic `ranges::merge`, whose final step unconditionally copies any leftover elements of the second range to the output (`copy(begin1, end1, out)`) once the first range is exhausted:\n\n```cpp\nauto t0 = ranges::copy(begin0, end0, out);\nauto t1 = ranges::copy(begin1, end1, t0.out);\n```\n\nIn this call, the \"first range\" (`begin0`/`end0`) is the temporary buffer, and the \"second range\" (`begin1`/`end1`) is the *unbuffered* run that shares storage with `out`. Because the buffer holds exactly `len1` elements and `out` starts exactly `len1` positions behind `begin1`, the output cursor `out` always reaches `begin1`'s current position at the exact moment the buffer is exhausted. At that point the trailing `copy(begin1, end1, out)` executes `*out = *begin1` with `out == begin1` for every remaining element — i.e. `a[i] = std::move(a[i])`, a self-move-assignment for each remaining element.\n\nFor scalar types this is a harmless no-op, which is why the existing test suite (which exercises `int` arrays almost exclusively, even at N > 256) never caught it. But for `std::string` and other types with observable moved-from state, this silently empties the element — exactly the corruption reported in #1848. Credit to @brevzin's comment on the issue for isolating the self-move-assignment pattern; this PR pins down where in the algorithm it occurs and why.\n\n## Fix\n\n`merge_adaptive_fn::impl` now uses its own merge loop (`merge_no_tail_copy`) instead of the generic `ranges::merge`. It stops as soon as the buffered range is exhausted, without touching the remaining unbuffered elements — they are already sitting in their correct final position, since `out` has caught up to them. This mirrors how libc++'s `__merge_move_assign` handles the equivalent in-place merge in `std::stable_sort`. Both directions of `impl` (buffering the left run vs. the right run via reverse iterators) are updated the same way.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- Reproduced the corruption locally first, before making any code change, with a standalone program sorting `std::vector<std::string>` (long enough to defeat SSO) via `ranges::stable_sort` at various sizes > 256. Confirmed empty strings and an unsorted result on unmodified `master`.\n- Wrote a larger stress test (~8400 randomized trials, sizes 200–3000): **4985 failures** on unmodified `master` (some losing 1000+ elements to empty strings in a single sort), **0 failures** after the fix.\n- Added a regression test to `test/algorithm/stable_sort.cpp` (`test_stable_sort_moved_from_regression`) using randomized `std::string` vectors at several sizes above the 256-element adaptive threshold. Verified this new test **fails** on unmodified `master` (`CHECK failed \"std::is_sorted(...)\"`, `CHECK failed \"!s.empty()\"`) and **passes** with the fix applied.\n- Built and ran the full `stable_sort`, `inplace_merge`, `merge`, `sort`, and `stable_partition` test targets after the fix; all pass with no regressions.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/issues/1865/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ericniebler/range-v3/issues/1865/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]